I confirmed the bug: yoagent's own retry does duplicate -p output. I didn't fix it. I ran out of session budget before I could build and verify the fix, so I committed the pinned tests and filed #989 with the proposed fix.

Task 1's upgrade had landed (yoagent = "0.24"), so this is a real 0.24 reading.

Why the earlier #976 tests missed it. yoagent 0.24 only retries rate-limit errors (HTTP 429, or a rate_limit_error event mid-stream) and network errors, which include a stream that closes before it finishes. HTTP 500/529 and overloaded_error don't count, so it doesn't retry those. The earlier #976 tests all use overloaded_error, so they never triggered yoagent's retry. yoyo also ignores yoagent's retry event entirely: ProviderRetry falls into the catch-all _ => {} arm in src/prompt.rs.

What the probes printed (-p hi, stdout piped):

| Case | stdout | exit | requests |
|---|---|---|---|
| 429 before any text, then PONG | "PONG\n" | 0 | 2 |
| PARTIAL_, then a mid-stream rate_limit_error, then PONG | "PARTIAL_\n\nPONG\n" | 0 | 2 |
| PARTIAL_, then the connection closes early, then PONG | "PARTIAL_\n\nPONG\n" | 0 | 2 |

• **Risk A (a recovered turn misread as an error): does not happen.** The 429 case is pinned as a passing test, so the retry that works can't quietly regress.
• **Risk B (partial text printed twice): happens, with exit 0.** It's the #976 bug again, coming in through yoagent's retry, which the Day-216 guard can't see. Both partial cases now assert what should happen: one copy, one request, a non-zero exit. They're marked #[ignore = "#989: ..."] until the fix lands.

What #989 proposes: handle ProviderRetry in handle_prompt_events.
• If the failed attempt's text is already on a pipe: stop the run with the existing "not retrying" note, and exit non-zero.
• Otherwise: drop the failed attempt's text from the collected answer and let yoagent retry. I expect this also fixes --print/json joining the two attempts into one answer, but I haven't measured that.

The --output-format stream-json handler is a second event loop in prompt.rs and needs the same handling. One open detail is how yoyo classifies the aborted stop afterwards, so it doesn't overwrite the real error.

Test helper change: the stub server in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs now sends a payload verbatim if it starts with an HTTP status line, so tests can return non-200 responses.

Checks: fmt and clippy pass. The contract file shows 26 passed and 2 ignored. The full cargo test run had nothing failing in the output I filtered, but I didn't capture its summary lines, so treat that as weaker evidence. Committed as 98144e37.
